# SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159  -  CAT II
# Warning and error messages displayed to clients must be modified to
# minimize the identity of the web server, patches, loaded modules, and
# directory paths.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159
group:           V-206412
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001312
control_rev5:    SI-11

contribution:    The check text looks for a mode of operation that minimizes the
                 information returned to clients on error conditions, and Splunk Web offers
                 exactly that choice: simple_error_page selects a page carrying only the
                 HTTP error status in place of a verbose page, request.show_tracebacks
                 suppresses the Python traceback that would disclose loaded module names
                 and installation paths, and appServerProcessLogStderr keeps application
                 server standard error — which the specification warns may carry session
                 identifier strings — out of the Splunk log.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] simple_error_page equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] request.show_tracebacks equals false
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] appServerProcessLogStderr https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] request.show_tracebacks https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] simple_error_page https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] appServerProcessLogStderr not_equals true
                 reason: "If set to true, messages written to the standard error stream by
                         the Python-based application server processes will be logged to
                         splunkd.log under the 'UiAppServer' channel. This can be useful
                         when debugging issues when the appserver process fails to start.
                         However, some appserver code may print sensitive information such
                         as session ID strings to standard error so this defaults to
                         disabled. Default: false"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Product identification carried in HTTP response headers and on the login
                 page: no key in the examined specification set strips Splunk's own
                 identification from those surfaces, so header rewriting and banner
                 suppression are carried by the reverse proxy or load balancer fronting
                 Splunk.
external:        Error pages and warning text rendered by custom apps, dashboards and
                 custom REST handlers: their templates are carried by the app developer and
                 the app approval process, not by web.conf.
external:        Protection of the splunkd.log content that application server standard
                 error lands in — file permissions, retention and onward forwarding — is
                 carried by the host operating system and the log management baseline.

citation:        SRG-APP-000266-WSR-000159 check and fix text (CCI-001312, SI-11 a); no
                 product STIG rule shares CCI-001312. Splunk 10.x specification set
                 (Version 10.0.0): web.conf.spec:227 simple_error_page, default false,
                 contrasting a page containing only the error status against a verbose page
                 containing the home link, message, results link, crashes, referrer, debug
                 output and byline; web.conf.spec:910 request.show_tracebacks, default
                 true, controlling whether an exception traceback is displayed to the user
                 on fatal exceptions; web.conf.spec:1285 appServerProcessLogStderr, default
                 false, whose text warns that appserver code may print sensitive
                 information such as session ID strings to standard error.
finding:         Splunk Web is not in its information-minimizing mode — web.conf [settings]
                 simple_error_page is not true, request.show_tracebacks is not false, or
                 appServerProcessLogStderr is true — so error responses carry the verbose
                 page's debug output, referrer, crash and byline detail, or a Python
                 traceback disclosing loaded modules and installation paths; this is
                 assessed at the application layer alone, and product identification in
                 HTTP response headers and error templates supplied by custom apps are
                 recorded as external dependencies rather than as part of this finding.
